{"name":"Warm Embrace","hex":"#93817e","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"warm","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a somewhat high temperature, often but not always connoting that the high temperature is pleasant rather than uncomfortable.","Friendly and with affection."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To make or keep warm.","To become warm, to heat up."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/warm"},{"term":"embrace","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To clasp (someone or each other) in the arms with affection; to take in the arms; to hug.","To seize (something) eagerly or with alacrity; to accept or take up with cordiality; to welcome."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An act of putting arms around someone and bringing the person close to the chest; a hug.","An enclosure partially or fully surrounding someone or something."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/embrace"}],"entries":[],"images":[],"sounds":{"warm":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/36/En-us-warm.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/3/36/En-us-warm.ogg/En-us-warm.ogg.mp3"}],"embrace":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/63/En-uk-embrace.oga?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/6/63/En-uk-embrace.oga/En-uk-embrace.oga.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/ce/En-us-embrace.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/c/ce/En-us-embrace.ogg/En-us-embrace.ogg.mp3"},{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://